  "intro": {
    "cards": [
      {
        "title": "Present simple vs continuous",
        "title_cz": "Přítomný prostý a průběhový",
        "points": [
          "**Aspect** (aspekt) is not *when*. It is how you look at something.",
          "**Simple**: a habit, or something that is true.",
          "**Continuous**: now, for a short time. It will stop.",
          "Czech *pije* is both. English is not."
        ],
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Meaning",
            "Say"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "**simple**",
              "habit · a fact",
              "I **work**"
            ],
            [
              "**continuous**",
              "now · a short time",
              "I **am working**"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Same verb",
        "title_cz": "Stejné sloveso",
        "text_first": true,
        "points": [
          "Keep the **same** verb. Change the **form**.",
          "she / he → **-s** in simple: **drinks**.",
          "now → **be** + **-ing**: **is drinking**."
        ],
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "every day",
            "now"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "She **drinks** coffee every morning.",
              "Look! She **is drinking** coffee."
            ],
            [
              "We **play** every Sunday.",
              "Look! We **are playing** now."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Some verbs stay simple",
        "title_cz": "Některá slovesa zůstávají v simple",
        "text_first": true,
        "points": [
          "**know, like, want, have** (got) — not a short action.",
          "Not *I am knowing*. Not *she is liking*.",
          "That is still **present simple** — the form you already know."
        ],
        "table": {
          "headers": [
            "Not",
            "Say"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "*I am knowing*",
              "I **know**"
            ],
            [
              "*She is liking coffee*",
              "She **likes** coffee"
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
